[38;5;231m⏺[39m I've opened a browser companion to show where the filters could go. It should have opened on its own. If it didn't,
  use this URL: [94m]8;id=894cnk;http://localhost:64993/?key=65e484243d3fe7a5de9927a1bcee8ab04ec4cfa39b29d1cffc0fdb10951739a4\http://localhost:64993/?key=65e484243d3fe7a5de9927a1bcee8ab04ec4cfa39b29d1cffc0fdb10951739a4[39m]8;;\

  Mockups use more tokens than plain chat, so I'll only use the companion for questions about layout.

  The screen has three wireframes. Each has the same filters and a live count like "Showing 9 of 48 events":
  - A: a compact row above the table. One Event select offers All events, Failed sign-ins, Security changes, then the
    nine types, so it filters one choice at a time. The date range sits beside it. This is the smallest diff.
  - B: a panel above the table, always visible. Shortcut buttons sit above a checkbox list of all nine types, then the
    dates. Any mix of types works, but the table moves down about 150px.
  - C: a "Filters" button that opens a popover, with removable tags showing what's active. The table stays high on the
    page, but failed sign-ins take an extra click.

  I lean toward A. Both requests you described ("failed sign-ins" and "security changes in one week") work as a single
  choice plus dates, and A needs the least code.

  The mockup files are in [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m in the repo root, which isn't gitignored. I'll keep them out of every commit.

  Click an option in the browser if you like, then tell me here which layout you want.

